      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>1 · HAVE / HAS</b> <span class='es'>— tener</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "I have a brother.",
              "sp": "Tengo un hermano. Igual con <b>you / we / they</b>: <i>We have a dog.</i>"
            },
            {
              "en": "She has a sister.",
              "sp": "Ella tiene una hermana. Con <b>he / she / it</b> → <b>has</b>."
            },
            {
              "en": "Tom has a car.",
              "sp": "Tom tiene un auto. Un nombre = he/she → <b>has</b>."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "<ico-warn></ico-warn> have o has",
              "body": "I / you / we / they → <code>have</code> &nbsp;·&nbsp; he / she / it → <code>has</code><br><s class='x'>She have a dog.</s> → <span class='ok'>She has a dog.</span>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>2 · NO Y PREGUNTAS</b> <span class='es'>— con don't / doesn't y do / does</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "I don't have a car.",
              "sp": "No tengo auto."
            },
            {
              "en": "She doesn't have a pet.",
              "sp": "Ella no tiene mascota. Con he/she → <b>doesn't</b>."
            },
            {
              "en": "Do you have a pet?",
              "sp": "¿Tienes mascota?"
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, I do. / No, I don't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No. — la respuesta corta usa <b>do</b>, no have."
            },
            {
              "en": "Does he have a job?",
              "sp": "¿Él tiene trabajo?"
            },
            {
              "en": "Yes, he does. / No, he doesn't.",
              "sp": "Sí. / No."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>Después de doesn't o does, vuelve have</b> (nunca has): <s class='x'>She doesn't has</s> → <span class='ok'>She doesn't have</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <s class='x'>Does he has…?</s> → <span class='ok'>Does he have…?</span><br>Y la respuesta corta no repite have: <s class='x'>Yes, I have.</s> → <span class='ok'>Yes, I do.</span>"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "html": "<b style='color:var(--cyan);display:inline-block;margin-top:14px'>3 · LA FAMILIA</b>"
        },
        {
